2. Non-commercial research

The copyright holders grant permission, without a license fee, to download,
copy, use, and modify the Materials solely for non-commercial research.
Existing copyright notices and this license must be retained in copies and
modifications of the Materials. Modifying the Materials does not remove the
commercial-use restriction.

Non-commercial research means research whose use of the Materials is not
intended to generate commercial advantage or revenue. The status of the user
as a university, nonprofit, company, or individual does not by itself decide
whether a particular use is non-commercial.

This license permits publication of research findings obtained through the
permitted use of the Materials. It does not grant rights to third-party data
used with the Materials.

3. Commercial use

Commercial use of the Materials or modifications requires prior written
